  "narrative": {
    "intro": "California Institute of Technology has federal contract obligations of $2.1B for FY2026 to date, distributed across 393 awards with an average award size of $5.3M. California Institute of Technology's obligations are down 9.3% year over year. California Institute of Technology received obligations of $2.3B in FY21, $2.6B in FY22, $2.7B in FY23, $2.2B in FY24, $2.3B in FY25, and $2.1B in FY26. California Institute of Technology's largest reported market is Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) with $2.1B in obligations. California Institute of Technology's current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. California Institute of Technology's figures here are contract obligations except where award-value tables are explicitly noted as total contract values. California Institute of Technology's award count and average award size show a portfolio concentrated in larger, research-focused awards rather than many small transactions. California Institute of Technology's year-over-year decline signals a smaller obligations tally so far in FY2026 compared with the prior fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
